  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 AM CDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nA stagnant dome of high pressure over the southeast U.S. will \ncontinue to keep very hot and humid air across the PAH forecast area \nthe rest the week.  High temperatures will continue to be mostly in \nthe middle 90s with dew points in the middle to upper 70s through \nFriday.  Max heat index readings today through Thursday will range \nfrom 105 to possibly near 115 degrees. \n\nBy Thursday and even more so Friday, the center of the high \nwill be pushing eastward, allowing weak perturbations in the \nupper flow to move over the middle Mississippi and lower Ohio \nvalleys. This will give our area 20-30% chances of showers and \nstorms Thursday afternoon and evening, and 30-40% chances Friday\nafternoon and night. Chances of 30-50% will continue through \nthe weekend into Monday, with the highest chances during the\nafternoon/early evening hours.\n\nThe additional clouds and scattered showers and storms will \nbring temperatures down a couple of degrees, and heat indices\nwill trend down a little over the weekend. Heat index readings\nSaturday and Sunday will be mostly in the 100 to 105 degrees.\nRain chances Monday are associated with a potential cold front,\nand depending on the timing, conditions will become a little\nmore tolerable early next week.",
